# No foreign repo / product names in ODS

Do **not** write names of other companies, products, monorepos, or client codebases into ODS repository files (code, specs, tests, docs, comments, commit messages that land in the repo, fixtures READMEs, i18n).

## Use instead

- Generic labels: `large-monorepo`, `sample app`, `external pilot repo`, `operator local path`
- Synthetic paths in tests: `Large.Monorepo.App/...`, `/absolute/path/to/...`
- ODS-owned names only: `ods-architecture`, fixture dirs under `docker/fixtures/repos/*`

## Examples

```text
❌ Named third-party products, client monorepos, or org paths from another codebase
✅ large-monorepo smoke; Large.Monorepo.App/modules/.../file.ts
```

## Scope

- Applies to anything committed or proposed for commit under this repo.
- Local-only files that are gitignored (e.g. `docker/.env`) may use real host paths for the operator machine; still avoid pasting third-party product names into tracked examples (`.env.example`, specs, tests).
- Chat with the user may name external repos when discussing their machine; do not copy those names into project artifacts.
